amplican 1.35.6
-----------------------
    o Handle missing forward-primer offsets when extracting reverse-only reads.
    o Preserve valid empty results when assembling fully filtered alignments.
    o Extend upstream truth tests and mutation checks for assignment, orientation,
      read multiplicities, batching, sampling, resume, and parallel execution.
    o Clarify that primer matching uses the best overlap alignment.
    o Count paired control evidence once per read/event during normalization.
      The control-frequency threshold remains strictly greater than min_freq.
    o Correct relative cut-site overlap when a nonzero cut buffer is used.
    o Recognize zero-start relative events in primer-overlap filtering.
    o Resolve disagreements between two clipped reads without strand bias.
    o Aggregate off-target features and safety-cap counts once per read.
      Cached filtered/normalized event tables and summaries require regeneration.
    o Extend core decision tests and the developer mutation audit.

amplican 1.35.5
-----------------------
    o Correct mismatch reference and replacement labels around insertions,
      including label reassignment between reads. Existing event tables require
      regeneration to receive this correction.

amplican 1.31.2
-----------------------
    o major changes to amplican way of finding primers, it should be way faster and more robust
    o some small fixes to make findLQR more robust
    o findLQR is ~9x faster (CLARA samples reduced from 500 to 50) with no
      change to the off-target decision on real and synthetic fixtures
    o findLQR now passes rngR = TRUE to CLARA so the seed argument actually
      controls reproducibility (previously a no-op)

amplican 1.5.8
-----------------------
    o amplican has been published now, doi: 10.1101/gr.244293.118
    o clearly outperforms other tools on many benchmarks
    o please cite the paper if you ar eusing amplican

amplican 1.1.3
-----------------------
    o fixed couple bugs
    o improved HDR
    o HDR for base editors
    o example of HDR
    o FAQ vignette

amplican 1.1.2
-----------------------

    o ampliCan supports now other aligners with SAM format eg. bwa mem
    (cigarsToEvents) and pair format eg. EMBOSS needleall (pairToEvents)
    o HDR quantification
    o more then 10x speed up of extracting events from alignments

